  "query_preview": "/Thursday through Monday/...\nThe warm, dry weather will continue Thursday with high temps \nwell into the 80s in the lower valleys and 75 to 85 in the\nmountains. Later Thursday a new upper trough will dig southward\nalong the BC coast. The trough will push a dry surface cold \nfront southeastward through our CWA Thursday night. The front \nwill bring gusty winds from the west or northwest, followed by \ncooler, breezy weather Friday through Sunday, with Sunday likely \nas cool as today. The supporting upper trough will bring a chance\nof showers to our northern mountain zones Saturday and Sunday, \nwith snow level near 8000 feet.",
